    vision_instruction: `\n\nSERVICE VISUAL GATE — EXTERIOR CONCRETE STAIR FORMWORK (Escalier béton en cours)\n\nYou are assessing a small ground-supported exterior concrete entrance stair that is being actively formed in front of a residential doorway. The scene MUST show a compact stair with 3 or 4 steps, wooden formwork panels defining each step, the formwork resting directly on a compacted base, and one mason adjusting the formwork from ground level. No concrete should yet fill all the steps.\n\nReturn every field listed below exactly once. Every field must be either true or false. Never omit a field. Never return null, unknown, unclear, or not_applicable. When evidence is not visible, return false.\n\nField definitions:\n- residential_building_entrance_visible: true if a residential building facade with an exterior door, French door, or bay window opening is clearly visible in the background — the stair clearly serves this entrance; false if no building or door is visible\n- small_exterior_concrete_stair_context_visible: true if the overall scene coherently shows a small exterior residential entrance stair context — compact stepped access between ground level and a doorway, outdoor setting, residential scale; false if the scene shows an interior stair, a monumental stair, a ramp, or no stair context at all\n- stepped_stair_formwork_visible: true if wooden or metal formwork boards defining clearly stepped stair profiles are the dominant structural element in the scene — distinct horizontal tread and vertical riser shapes visible; false if formwork is absent or is a single flat board (threshold)\n- distinct_riser_boards_visible: true if individual vertical riser boards are clearly visible as separate horizontal boards nailed across the step width at each step height — at least 2 or 3 individual riser boards distinguishable; false if no riser boards are visible or only a single board is present\n- side_formwork_panels_visible: true if at least one lateral side panel (in wood or equivalent) is clearly visible flanking the stair profile from the bottom to the top step — defining the width of the stair on at least one side; false if no side panels are visible\n- three_or_four_step_profile_visible: true if the stepped profile of exactly 3 or 4 steps is clearly visible — count the distinct step levels and confirm the count is 3 or 4; false if fewer than 3 or more than 4 steps are visible, or if the profile is not clearly stepped\n- ground_supported_compacted_base_visible: true if the formwork base clearly rests on the existing ground or a visible compacted gravel or earth base — the stair is built directly on the ground surface, not suspended; false if no ground contact is visible or the formwork appears suspended\n- formwork_bracing_or_stakes_visible: true if wooden stakes, metal pins, timber braces, or equivalent supports are clearly visible anchoring or bracing the side panels or riser boards — preventing movement during the pour; false if no bracing or stakes are visible\n- active_stair_formwork_adjustment_visible: true if the single visible worker is clearly and actively adjusting, positioning, or fixing a component of the stair formwork — holding a board in place, hammering a nail, tightening a brace, or checking alignment with a tool — confirming work in progress; false if no active adjustment is visible or the worker is simply standing observing\n- worker_stable_at_ground_level: true if the single visible worker is standing, crouching, or kneeling on the natural ground or stable surface beside or at the base of the stair formwork — not elevated, not on the formwork, not on reinforcement; false if the worker is elevated or standing on the formwork or rebar\n- worker_standing_on_formwork: true ONLY if a worker is clearly standing with both feet on top of the wooden formwork boards — a direct safety risk; set true if this hazard is clearly visible\n- worker_standing_on_rebar: true ONLY if a worker is clearly standing on reinforcement bars — set true if this hazard is clearly visible\n- suspended_stair_formwork_visible: true ONLY if the stair formwork is clearly suspended between two elevated floors with no ground support visible — typical of an interior staircase between storeys; set true if the formwork has no visible ground contact at all\n- fresh_concrete_filling_all_steps_visible: true ONLY if fresh wet concrete is clearly visible filling all steps — confirming the pour is already complete or in progress for all treads simultaneously; set true if all treads are clearly filled with fresh concrete\n- large_slab_area_dominant: true ONLY if a large horizontal concrete slab covering a broad surface area (dalle béton, terrasse béton) is clearly the dominant element — a compact stair with 3–4 steps does NOT qualify as a large slab area\n- threshold_only_work_visible: true ONLY if the formwork visible is clearly a single narrow threshold at the base of a door with no stepped profile — a flat single-level form at floor level only; set true if no stepped levels are visible\n- lintel_work_visible: true ONLY if a lintel beam spanning a wall opening at elevated height above the ground is clearly the primary work element — a door or window lintel installation\n- service_visual_match: true if the scene coherently shows an exterior residential entrance stair being actively formed — 3 or 4 stepped levels, wooden formwork panels with individual riser boards, ground-supported compacted base, formwork bracing visible, one worker actively adjusting from ground level, building entrance visible in background, no concrete yet filling all steps; false if the scene shows a large slab, a simple threshold, a lintel, an interior stair, a finished stair, or a stair without active formwork work\n- worker_count_match: true if the number of clearly visible active workers matches the planned count (var_workers)\n\nReturn ONLY valid JSON with exactly these 19 fields, all as booleans:\n{"residential_building_entrance_visible": <bool>, "small_exterior_concrete_stair_context_visible": <bool>, "stepped_stair_formwork_visible": <bool>, "distinct_riser_boards_visible": <bool>, "side_formwork_panels_visible": <bool>, "three_or_four_step_profile_visible": <bool>, "ground_supported_compacted_base_visible": <bool>, "formwork_bracing_or_stakes_visible": <bool>, "active_stair_formwork_adjustment_visible": <bool>, "worker_stable_at_ground_level": <bool>, "worker_standing_on_formwork": <bool>, "worker_standing_on_rebar": <bool>, "suspended_stair_formwork_visible": <bool>, "fresh_concrete_filling_all_steps_visible": <bool>, "large_slab_area_dominant": <bool>, "threshold_only_work_visible": <bool>, "lintel_work_visible": <bool>, "service_visual_match": <bool>, "worker_count_match": <bool>}`,
